A||N||2||KRMFiero||Just a quick Question(s) on Fastback Conversions||||1||
Z||000000||KRMFiero||04-28-2001||10:51 AM||||Hi, Okay I might be getting a Fastback, Decklid.... I currently have the 84 Bumpers and molding on    would the fastback fit on with those bumpers,  when I get more oney what bumpers would look the best on it, would like a 87 coupe style look good? how hard is it to put ground effects on if i get GT bumpers?<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||mbramble||04-28-2001||12:06 PM||||Any of the bumper covers will fit any of the cars.<P>If you just buy the ground effects pieces and their mounting hardware, you will have to drill mounting holes in your non-f/x panels.  I just did this for a front fender I picked up at the junkyard.  Of course I had the original one that I made a template from to locate the holes correctly.  Without having panels drilled for the f/x pieces you will need to do a bit of measuring to drill each panel so the f/x pieces will mount properly and not be crooked, off-center, etc.  Not difficult to do, just time-consuming.  Measure twice -- drill once!!  Though in reality, if you drill a hole in the wrong place it wouldn't show once you got the f/x piece attached (as long as the incorrect hole was in the area where the piece attaches!!<P>As far as which bumpers look good with the fastback, I guess it's mostly a matter of choice.  But, if you are going to install ground f/x, then you would want the bumpers that have the f/x moulded onto the bottom (85 GT, 86-87 SE, 86+GT, Indy)||||reg||1
Z||000002||danny boy||04-28-2001||12:11 PM|||| When buying bumpers make sure the moulding matches. 87-88 all and 86-88 GT round moulding, 84-86 all + 87 SE square.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
